     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"attack_techniques\": [{\"id\": \"T1071\", \"name\": \"Application Layer Protocol\", \"tactics\": [\"Command and Control\"], \"why_relevant\": \"The botnet C2 communication over TCP port 8080 likely uses an application layer protocol for command and control traffic between the infected host and remote C2 server.\"}, {\"id\": \"T1568.002\", \"name\": \"Domain Generation Algorithms\", \"tactics\": [\"Command and Control\"], \"why_relevant\": \"The connection to malware.botnet.ru domain queried in the alert suggests potential use of dynamic domain-based C2 infrastructure to maintain command and control communications.\"}, {\"id\": \"T1132.001\", \"name\": \"Standard Encoding\", \"tactics\": [\"Command and Control\"], \"why_relevant\": \"Botnet C2 traffic typically encodes commands and data using standard encoding schemes to evade detection while communicating with the remote C2 server.\"}], \"identity_signals\": null, \"key_findings\": \"An internal host (10.100.50.25) attempted to establish command and control communication with a known botnet infrastructure at malware.botnet.ru on port 8080, indicating potential malware infection. The firewall blocked the outbound connection, preventing C2 establishment. However, the presence of botnet C2 traffic from an internal endpoint suggests the host may already be compromised and attempting to communicate with malicious infrastructure.\", \"severity\": \"high\", \"severity_rationale\": \"This alert meets the high severity threshold because it involves activity originating from an internal host (10.100.50.25) attempting C2 communication with external malicious infrastructure. While the firewall blocked the outbound connection, the fact that an internal endpoint is actively attempting to reach a known botnet C2 server indicates potential malware infection or compromise on that host. This requires immediate investigation to determine if the host is infected and whether lateral movement or data exfiltration has occurred.\", \"confidence\": 0.95, \"recommended_response\": \"Immediately isolate the internal host 10.100.50.25 from the network to prevent potential malware propagation and further C2 communication attempts. Perform a full forensic analysis and malware scan of the endpoint to confirm infection status and identify any additional compromise indicators. Review network logs for lateral movement attempts or data exfiltration from this host. Check for similar C2 connection attempts from other internal hosts that may indicate widespread botnet infection. Notify the asset owner and begin incident response procedures.\", \"rounds_used\": 0}",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
