 "a54d0464f7698001": [
  {
   "container": null,
   "content": [
    {
     "citations": null,
     "text": "{\"attack_techniques\":[],\"identity_signals\":null,\"key_findings\":\"A firewall rule blocked outbound TCP traffic to a known botnet C2 domain (malware.botnet.ru) on port 8080 originating from internal IP 10.100.50.25 with 98% confidence. The connection attempt was denied at the perimeter, preventing any successful C2 communication. No identity signals or authentication anomalies were detected.\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"severity_rationale\":\"This alert represents a blocked attack attempt at the network perimeter. While the destination has known malicious reputation and the detection confidence is high, the firewall action (blocked) prevented successful C2 communication and there is no evidence of compromise on the internal host or successful command execution. The activity did not reach the destination and poses no immediate internal risk.\",\"confidence\":0.98,\"recommended_response\":\"Investigate the source endpoint (10.100.50.25) for malware presence using EDR tools; scan for artifacts of botnet infection or suspicious processes. If malware is confirmed, isolate the host and perform forensic analysis. If clean, investigate how the domain became queried (browser history, DNS logs, proxies). Monitor the internal IP for further C2 communication attempts. Consider whether the host needs re-imaging or remediation.\",\"rounds_used\":0}",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "diagnostics": null,
   "id": "msg_011ChA5NVxgxjUJSk7PX7Toh",
