     "text": "{\"completeness\": 0.85, \"citation_quality\": 0.65, \"severity_defensibility\": 0.90, \"overall_pass\": false, \"feedback\": \"The investigation demonstrates strong severity assessment and comprehensive recommended response actions, but has two notable gaps. First, the ATT&CK technique citations need better justification\u2014T1568.002 (Domain Generation Algorithms) is questionable since the alert involves a static known domain (malware.botnet.ru), not algorithmic generation, and T1132.001 (Standard Encoding) lacks any evidence in the provided data; only T1071 (Application Layer Protocol) is clearly applicable for C2 traffic. Second, the investigation lacks identity/account context entirely\u2014there is no mention of which user/account is associated with the compromised host 10.100.50.25, whether it's a user workstation or server, or any investigation into user behavior. Add proper justification for each ATT&CK technique selection and include investigation of the asset owner, user accounts, and logon activity on the affected endpoint to establish full context.\"}",
